  "strategy": null,
  "job_description": "VP, Global Construction Execution (EMEA)\n\nNTT is currently looking for a Vice President, Global Construction Execution (EMEA) (m/f/d). The Vice President, Global (EMEA) is a key executive role reporting directly to the Vice President Global Construction. The successful candidate will be responsible for the construction of capital infrastructure investment in EMEA. Playing a critical role in overseeing and managing construction projects for the organization. Providing strategic direction and leadership to ensure successful project delivery within specified timelines, budgets, and quality standards.\n\nThis is a full time hybrid role based in the UK, Germany or Netherlands.\n\nWhat you will do:\n- Project Management: Lead and oversee construction projects from initiation to completion, ensuring adherence to project plans, schedules, and budgets. Monitor progress, identify potential risks, and implement mitigation strategies as necessary.\n- Strategic Planning: Develop and implement strategic plans for the construction department, aligning with the organization's overall goals and objectives. Identify opportunities for growth, process improvement, and cost optimization.\n- Team Leadership: Manage and mentor a team of construction professionals, including project managers, engineers, architects, and contractors. Foster a collaborative and high-performing work environment, promoting teamwork and individual development.\n- Vendor and Contractor Management: Liaisons with supply chain to evaluate performance of general contractors and other suppliers to ensure compliance execution, quality, and safety standards.\n- Budgeting and Financial Management: Liaisons with project controls to in reporting to senior management, highlighting project performance and potential risks.\n- Quality Assurance: Work with CX/Quality team to ensure quality assurance programs are construction met or exceed industry standards and regulatory requirements. Monitor compliance with building codes, safety regulations, and environmental guidelines.\n- Stakeholder Communication: Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders, including clients, architects, engineers, and regulatory authorities. Communicate project updates, resolve issues, and maintain positive relationships with all parties involved.\n\nWhat we are looking for:\n- Extensive experience (15+ years) in construction management, preferably in a leadership role within the construction industry.\n- Bachelor's degree in construction management, Civil Engineering, or a related field. Master's degree (beneficial).\n- Strong knowledge of construction methodologies, building codes, safety regulations, and industry best practices.\n- Proven track record of successfully delivering complex construction projects on time and within budget.\n- Strong financial acumen and experience in budgeting, cost control, and financial analysis.\n- Proficiency in project management software, construction management tools, and MS Office suite.\n- Understanding of engineering/engineering background.\n- Proven experience in implementing processes in a rapid growth environment.\n- Knowledgeable of the principals of operating in compliance with each state where NTT is located and Federal OSHA standards and regulations.\n- Knowledgeable of construction law and contracts.\n- Skilled at developing and understanding critical path method construction schedules.\n- Skilled at creating and maintaining a collaborative design/construction/operations environment in a global culture.",
  "job_requirements": null,
